{"question_id": "A-01", "arm": "openmcp", "requested_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "model_ids": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "tools_available": ["mcp__openmcp__get_dataset", "mcp__openmcp__get_file_schema", "mcp__openmcp__get_resource_fields", "mcp__openmcp__list_excel_sheets", "mcp__openmcp__preview_remote_file", "mcp__openmcp__query_boc_valet", "mcp__openmcp__query_datastore", "mcp__openmcp__query_excel_sheet", "mcp__openmcp__query_remote_file", "mcp__openmcp__query_statcan_wds", "mcp__openmcp__read_pdf", "mcp__openmcp__search_datasets", "mcp__openmcp__semantic_search_datasets"], "started_at": "2026-11-10T03:27:10+00:00", "duration_s": 153.5, "tool_calls": ["mcp__openmcp__query_statcan_wds", "mcp__openmcp__query_statcan_wds", "mcp__openmcp__query_remote_file", "mcp__openmcp__query_remote_file", "mcp__openmcp__query_remote_file", "mcp__openmcp__query_remote_file", "mcp__openmcp__get_file_schema", "mcp__openmcp__query_remote_file"], "is_error": false, "response": "In 2024, the latest year published, **12.8% of Alberta children under 18 were in low income**. That is about 135,500 children, measured with the Market Basket Measure (2023 base), which is Canada's official poverty line. This rate is up from 11.9% in 2023 and 12.0% in 2022.\n\nThe Low Income Measure (after tax) gives a different figure of 13.9% for 2024, or about 147,300 children. Which one you use depends on the definition of poverty you want.\n\nSource: Statistics Canada, Table 11-10-0135-01, \"Low income statistics by age, sex and economic family type\". The Market Basket Measure percentage is vector v1792632015, and the Low Income Measure percentage is v96520326. Reference period: 2024.\n\n```json\n{\"values\": [\n{\"name\": \"Alberta child (under 18) poverty rate, Market Basket Measure 2023 base\", \"value\": 12.8, \"unit\": \"%\", \"period\": \"2024\"},\n{\"name\": \"Alberta children under 18 in low income, MBM\", \"value\": 135500, \"unit\": \"persons\", \"period\": \"2024\"},\n{\"name\": \"Alberta child MBM rate\", \"value\": 11.9, \"unit\": \"%\", \"period\": \"2023\"},\n{\"name\": \"Alberta child MBM rate\", \"value\": 12.0, \"unit\": \"%\", \"period\": \"2022\"},\n{\"name\": \"Alberta child low income rate, LIM after tax\", \"value\": 13.9, \"unit\": \"%\", \"period\": \"2024\"}\n],\n\"sources\": [{\"publisher\": \"Statistics Canada\", \"id\": \"Table 11-10-0135-01; vectors v1792632015 (MBM %), v96520326 (LIM-AT %)\"}],\n\"not_published\": false,\n\"abstain\": false,\n\"abstain_reason\": \"\"}\n```", "repeat": 0, "cost_usd": 0.09992129999999999, "input_tokens": 16, "output_tokens": 2113, "cache_read_tokens": 71873, "cache_creation_tokens": 17893}
